Subject: [overlay 0033] eye-independent dynamic-light culling

Third headset verdict follow-up: walls flip light<->dark while walking slowly past
them, and sometimes only in ONE eye. Mechanism, file:line verified:

  * the rerelease's shadowlights are real dlight_t's, re-added every frame from static map
    entities (src/client/effects.c, V_AddLightEx in src/client/view.c), and
    gl_per_pixel_lighting defaults to 1 — so ALL of that light goes through the ppl UBO;
  * shader_load_lights culls each dlight with GL_CullSphere, which does `radius *=
    glr.entscale`;
  * glr.entscale is written ONLY by GL_SetEntityAxis and is never reset for the world pass.
    During the world draw it holds whatever the LAST ENTITY of the PREVIOUS render left in
    it — eye 1 inherits eye 0's, eye 0 inherits the previous frame's eye 1 — and entity
    classification is per-eye frustum culled, so the last entity DIFFERS BETWEEN THE EYES.

A shrunk radius drops the light entirely, so a whole panel face is dark in one eye and lit in
the other, flipping as the player creeps past the boundary. A dlight is a world-space sphere
with a world-space radius; no entity's scale has anything to say about it.

Three changes:

  * GL_CullLightSphere (main.c, prototype in gl.h beside GL_CullSphere): GL_CullSphere with
    the entscale multiply removed, and CULL_IN unconditionally when q2vr.active — the two
    eyes have different frusta, so any per-eye survivor set is a per-eye lighting difference
    by construction;
  * shader_load_lights uses it;
  * R_RenderFrame invalidates gls.dlight_bits at the top of every render. GL_LoadLights
    reloads the dlight UBO only when that key differs from glr.ppl_dlight_bits — a key that
    says which lights are LIT and nothing about which eye culled them — so eye 1's first lit
    batch could otherwise keep the block eye 0 uploaded from eye 0's survivors. One UBO
    upload per render buys the question away.

Companion to 0030 (constant render count) and 0031 (idempotent repeat render); those fixed
WHEN the world is re-rendered, this fixes what the second render is allowed to see.

--- a/src/refresh/main.c
+++ b/src/refresh/main.c
@@ -223,6 +223,44 @@
     return cull;
 }
 
+// [vr overlay 0033] THE DLIGHT CULL, WHICH IS NOT THE ENTITY CULL.
+//
+// GL_CullSphere above multiplies the radius by glr.entscale, and entscale is written ONLY by
+// GL_SetEntityAxis — never reset for the world pass. During the world draw it therefore holds
+// whatever the LAST ENTITY of the PREVIOUS render left in it: in stereo, eye 1 inherits eye
+// 0's and eye 0 inherits the previous frame's eye 1, and because entity classification is
+// per-eye frustum culled, the last entity differs BETWEEN THE EYES. A shrunk radius makes
+// shader_load_lights drop the light entirely, so a whole panel face goes dark in one eye and
+// stays lit in the other, flipping as the player creeps past the boundary — the reported "walls
+// flip light and dark while walking slowly, sometimes one eye only".
+//
+// A dlight is a world-space sphere with a world-space radius; no entity's scale has anything
+// to say about it. This is GL_CullSphere with that multiply removed. In VR it culls nothing at
+// all: the two eyes have different frusta, so any per-eye survivor set is a per-eye lighting
+// difference by construction, and the shadowlight set is small enough that keeping all of it
+// is cheaper than a class of artefact that reads as a tracking bug.
+glCullResult_t GL_CullLightSphere(const vec3_t origin, float radius)
+{
+    const cplane_t *p;
+    glCullResult_t cull;
+    float dist;
+    int i;
+
+    if (!gl_cull_models->integer || q2vr.active)
+        return CULL_IN;
+
+    cull = CULL_IN;
+    for (i = 0, p = glr.frustumPlanes; i < 4; i++, p++) {
+        dist = PlaneDiff(origin, p);
+        if (dist < -radius)
+            return CULL_OUT;
+        if (dist <= radius)
+            cull = CULL_CLIP;
+    }
+
+    return cull;
+}
+
 glCullResult_t GL_CullLocalBox(const vec3_t origin, const vec3_t bounds[2])
 {
     vec3_t points[8];
@@ -879,6 +917,15 @@
     else
         glr.dlightframe_base = glr.dlightframe;
 
+    // [vr overlay 0033] FORCE THE PER-PIXEL-LIGHTING UBO TO RELOAD FOR THIS RENDER.
+    // GL_LoadLights reloads the dlight uniform block only when gls.dlight_bits differs from
+    // glr.ppl_dlight_bits — a key that says WHICH LIGHTS ARE LIT, and nothing about which eye
+    // culled them. Two renders of the same frame have the same bits, so eye 1's first lit
+    // batch could keep the block eye 0 uploaded (built from eye 0's frustum survivors), which
+    // is the same one-eye-dark artefact from the other end. Invalidating the key at the top of
+    // every render costs one UBO upload per render and removes the question.
+    gls.dlight_bits = ~(uint64_t)0;
+
     glr.fd = *fd;
     glr.ppl_bits  = 0;
 
